A||N||6||Monkeyman||Anyone have the Fiero Store fiberglass headliner board??||||9||
Z||000000||Monkeyman||11-15-2001||06:50 PM||||I bought Old Lars Fiero Store fiberglass headliner board.  I just covered it in a nice quality vinyl and installed it in my car.  I'm having a slight (but very frustrating) problem with the fit around the rear (towards the sunroof) of the overhead light console and the top of the windshield.  I have a hell (sorry) of a gap at the back of the overhead light console.  Probably a good 1/2".  Also, there's another 1/2" gap in between the front of the headliner and the top of the windshield.  Something's just not right.  One last little complaint.  I drilled the coat hook holes right where the little indentations were in the fiberglass.  Guess what?  Wrong place.  A drill bit will fix that, but someone at the Fiero Store didn't know how to use a ruler.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PontiacAPE.jpg">    <BR>Monkeyman||||reg||9
Z||000001||JohnF||11-15-2001||07:40 PM||||I've been told FS is the one to own!  That is the one I want.<P>This is a bump to see what we have here!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rodrv6||11-15-2001||07:56 PM||||I used the Fiero Stores kit in my 84 a few years ago.  On mine the fit was real good, although I did do a test fit before putting the headliner on it.  The holes for the sunvisor screws were good on one side and off on the other.  I don't think GM drilled them all in exactly the same place from car to car.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  <BR>White 88 GT :)||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||11-15-2001||10:22 PM||||MM, just so you know, Fiero Store does not make the fiberglass headliner board - they only sell them....... I get them from the same place they do and I have had to measure and pre-fit every one I have installed. I have found that the coat hook mounts have been mis-marked as much as 2 1/2" off!! Anbd, the visor mounting holes are not always accurate either. Just fit, trim, fit, trim and you will finally get it. I have been known to enlarge holes and trim once it is in place by using a sanding drum on a Dremel...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_TGO.jpg"> <P><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||LoW_KeY||11-15-2001||11:01 PM||||Heh you and me both.. I put mine in last year and the holes didn't line up! filled them back in and tried it again.. got it but barely kind of a rough fit.<P>Hope I don't have to pull the bugger back out again! that's one hell of a job I don't care to do again.  Not to mention I paid 100 to get someone to make the material stick 2 times and it never stuck for me! GRR  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>I think TFS should sell them with the material already put on along with the hole corrections  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kc.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||11-16-2001||03:14 AM||||I'll just drill some small holes in the roof for the coat hook screws.  I need those since I got rid of the 3<sup>rd</sup> brake light.  I'm actually more concerned with the way the front fits.  My car will never be perfect, but I'd like it to be presentable.  That gap between the top of the windshield and the front of the headliner is just plain unacceptable.  I can deal with the gap around the light pod.  I was planning on building my own out of wood anyway.  I'll just make it a little differently than stock.  <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/patriot.gif">    <BR><B><FONT COLOR="red">Proud</FONT> <FONT COLOR="white">to be an</FONT> <FONT COLOR="blue">American</FONT>!!</B>||||reg||1
Z||000006||PaulJK||11-16-2001||04:35 AM||||I'm due to pick up my headliner from the upholstery shop tomorrow. My original headliner shell was OK, but a little too fragile for me to deal with. The upholsterer told me vinyl was too heavy for the roof and would eventually fall down. You may consider this before you put vinyl up there. I was convinced enough to get regular cloth material.||||reg||1
